_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:03b107c2e02647cc593d97db4577ae3b0d78257bcf3e07b1d10e94398d8e7ad9","file":"preprints/a-torsion-free-hyperbolic-group-that-is-not-residually-finite-September-23-2026/build/paper.tex","line":66,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"4f0dd7fb5b6734a9ea06bd13a0e42a304dc4c5a0664919d758085a8d165feee3","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/a-torsion-free-hyperbolic-group-that-is-not-residually-finite-September-23-2026/build/paper.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:03b107c2e02647cc593d97db4577ae3b0d78257bcf3e07b1d10e94398d8e7ad9","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/a-torsion-free-hyperbolic-group-that-is-not-residually-finite-September-23-2026/build/paper.tex#L66"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:nonlinear}\nLet $G$ be the finitely generated torsion-free word-hyperbolic group constructed in Theorem~\\ref{thm:main}. For every commutative field $K$, every integer $n\\geq 1$, and every homomorphism $\\rho:G\\to\\mathrm{GL}_n(K)$,\n\\[\nR_f(G)\\subseteq\\ker\\rho.\n\\]\nConsequently, one fixed nonidentity element of $G$ is killed by all these representations, simultaneously over all such fields and dimensions. In particular, $G$ is not linear over any commutative field."}
